            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Medical Career in Africa</strong><br>\nIn 1913, at the age of 38, Schweitzer founded a hospital in Lambaréné, Gabon. He spent most of his life there, treating patients who suffered from diseases such as leprosy and sleeping sickness. His work was often challenging, but Schweitzer remained dedicated to his mission of service.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Theological Contributions</strong><br>\nBesides his work in medicine, Schweitzer was a profound theologian. He challenged traditional Christian thought with his book \"The Quest of the Historical Jesus,\" which critically examined the life and teachings of Jesus Christ. His work had a lasting impact on Christian theology and biblical scholarship.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Nobel Peace Prize</strong><br>\nIn 1952, Albert Schweitzer was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize for his philosophy of \"Reverence for Life\" and his work in promoting peace and understanding. The award highlighted his efforts to make the world a better place through compassion and care for others.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
