          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Writings and Legacy</strong><br>\nSchweitzer was a prolific writer, authoring many books on both music and theology. His works continue to inspire people around the world. His legacy is not only as a Nobel laureate but also as an individual who lived a life of service to humanity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Humanitarian Work</strong><br>\nSchweitzer's approach to life and his service in Africa had a significant influence on humanitarian efforts worldwide. His example led to a greater awareness and emphasis on providing medical care in remote parts of the world where it was most needed.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Death</strong><br>\nAlbert Schweitzer continued to work in his hospital in Gabon until his health declined. He passed away on September 4, 1965, but his work in Lambaréné continues to this day. The hospital he founded serves as a lasting testament to his commitment to humanity and medical service.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
